2026-09-27T04:47:58.7203637Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7204047Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7204693Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7205288Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7205526Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7206066Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7206350Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7206706Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7207485Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7208007Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7208270Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7208895Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7209284Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7209638Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7210504Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7211205Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7212711Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7213670Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7213941Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7214784Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7215794Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7216330Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7216902Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7217661Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7217914Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7218314Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7218529Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7220841Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7223186Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7223606Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7224465Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7225395Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7226496Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7227539Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7228372Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7228848Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7229558Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7230096Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7230387Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7232555Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7234914Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7236706Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7238274Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:58.7238643Z 
